WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.760 --> 00:00:06.050
After a quiet start, it seems that Amazon
is finally gearing up to return to J.R.R.

00:00:06.050 --> 00:00:07.220
Tolkien's Middle-Earth.

00:00:07.220 --> 00:00:11.820
From release schedules to casting choices,
and astronomical budgets to familiar filming

00:00:11.820 --> 00:00:16.080
locations, here's everything there is to know
about Amazon's upcoming Lord of the Rings

00:00:16.080 --> 00:00:17.080
series.

00:00:17.560 --> 00:00:21.560
When Tolkien fans learned that Middle Earth
would be coming to screens for the first time

00:00:21.580 --> 00:00:25.550
since Peter Jackson's Hobbit trilogy, it's
only natural that their first question would

00:00:25.550 --> 00:00:26.600
be: "When?"

00:00:26.600 --> 00:00:31.640
Sadly, an exact answer hasn't become clear
yet, as no official release date has yet been

00:00:31.640 --> 00:00:32.640
announced.

00:00:32.640 --> 00:00:36.430
However, there are a few pieces of information
that might offer a few clues as to when the

00:00:36.430 --> 00:00:37.729
series might drop.

00:00:37.729 --> 00:00:40.350
First and foremost, there's a legal factor
to all this.

00:00:40.350 --> 00:00:45.199
In an interview with The Hollywood Reporter,
Amazon chief Jennifer Salke confirmed that

00:00:45.199 --> 00:00:49.550
part of the deal for the rights included the
condition that the show had to be in production

00:00:49.550 --> 00:00:50.699
within two years.

00:00:50.699 --> 00:00:55.399
She added that the hope is to have the show
"on the air" by 2021, with some even hoping

00:00:55.399 --> 00:00:56.579
for 2020.

00:00:56.579 --> 00:01:01.089
While it may feel a long way off, you don't
simply conjure a project of this size and

00:01:01.089 --> 00:01:02.499
scope out of thin air.

00:01:02.499 --> 00:01:06.940
The idea that Amazon could be able to pull
the first season together within four years

00:01:06.940 --> 00:01:10.890
of purchasing the rights is about as good
as anyone could ask for — especially if

00:01:10.890 --> 00:01:13.960
you don't want to sacrifice quality along
the way.

00:01:14.000 --> 00:01:18.661
While exact budgets are always hard to pin
down, especially early on in production, there

00:01:18.661 --> 00:01:22.981
can be little doubt that Amazon's adventures
through Middle Earth are going to cost the

00:01:22.981 --> 00:01:24.340
studio a tidy sum.

00:01:24.340 --> 00:01:30.170
Right out of the gate, the rights alone cost
Bezos and company a whopping $250 million.

00:01:30.170 --> 00:01:34.610
As if that wasn't enough, rumors immediately
began swirling around how much Amazon planned

00:01:34.610 --> 00:01:36.940
on shelling out to actually make the show.

00:01:36.940 --> 00:01:41.430
Entertainment Weekly reported early in 2018
that the first two seasons alone were going

00:01:41.430 --> 00:01:45.300
to double the cost of the rights — that's
half a billion dollars.

00:01:45.300 --> 00:01:47.060
Since then, that number has only gone up.

00:01:47.060 --> 00:01:52.250
At this point, when all costs are considered,
a cool billion stands as one of the lower

00:01:52.250 --> 00:01:57.300
estimates out there, while others have pushed
the figure comfortably north of that mark.

00:01:57.300 --> 00:02:01.409
While it's easy to trot out the old line that
"it takes money to make money" — especially

00:02:01.409 --> 00:02:05.800
in an era rife with luxurious production budgets
— the idea of dropping somewhere in the

00:02:05.800 --> 00:02:11.280
neighborhood of $1.5 billion on a single television
show is about as excessive as it gets.

00:02:12.200 --> 00:02:17.680
Over the course of a few weeks in early 2019,
Amazon Studios posted a number of interactive

00:02:17.700 --> 00:02:22.090
maps to their official Twitter account, each
accompanied by new annotations and a line

00:02:22.090 --> 00:02:25.409
from the famous poem inscribed on the One
Ring.

00:02:25.409 --> 00:02:29.690
The first few depicted the Middle-Earth Lord
of the Rings fans will all know and love,

00:02:29.690 --> 00:02:34.099
albeit with a few hints that the maps actually
portrayed an earlier version of Tolkien's

00:02:34.099 --> 00:02:35.099
world.

00:02:35.099 --> 00:02:39.069
Rohan, for example, was labeled 'Calenardhon'
— the name of the Gondorian province that

00:02:39.069 --> 00:02:42.430
preceded Théoden's Rohan by at least 500
years.

00:02:42.440 --> 00:02:48.120
On March 7th 2019, Amazon Studios posted one
final map along with the last line of the

00:02:48.120 --> 00:02:49.120
poem:

00:02:49.160 --> 00:02:55.120
"One Ring to bring them all and in the darkness
bind them."

00:02:55.130 --> 00:02:59.510
The last map had a much wider view of the
world than had the previous versions, and

00:02:59.510 --> 00:03:03.829
this macro view of Middle Earth exposed one
critical piece of information in the bottom

00:03:03.829 --> 00:03:07.739
left corner that changed everything: the island
of Númenor.

00:03:07.739 --> 00:03:11.799
The reason this not-so-little island is a
big deal is because it only existed during

00:03:11.799 --> 00:03:14.439
the Second Age of Tolkien's mythology.

00:03:14.439 --> 00:03:18.260
Founded after the catastrophic war that ended
the First Age, the island nation served as

00:03:18.260 --> 00:03:23.069
a home for the Númenóreans, a society of
divinely-blessed humans that flourished during

00:03:23.069 --> 00:03:26.739
the Second Age — in fact, the Numenoreans
were the ones who founded the kingdoms of

00:03:26.739 --> 00:03:28.890
Gondor and Arnor on the mainland.

00:03:28.890 --> 00:03:33.779
But thanks to the disastrous rule of a tyrant
king and the influence of a certain ne'er-do-well

00:03:33.779 --> 00:03:38.790
called Sauron, the Numenoreans were destroyed
and their island sunk beneath the waves shortly

00:03:38.790 --> 00:03:40.510
before the Third Age began.

00:03:40.510 --> 00:03:45.269
Since Amazon's map depicts Númenor, it has
to mean that the studio's creative team has

00:03:45.269 --> 00:03:48.230
its sights firmly set on the Second Age.

00:03:48.230 --> 00:03:52.489
While there's been little other information
about the setting, the revelation that Númenor

00:03:52.489 --> 00:03:57.110
will exist during the show's run has brought
a new kind of excitement to the venture, as

00:03:57.110 --> 00:04:01.139
it means fans will get to experience a part
of Middle Earth history that has never before

00:04:01.139 --> 00:04:03.080
been explored on screen

00:04:03.360 --> 00:04:07.989
Considering this series will be such a huge
undertaking, you would think that Amazon would

00:04:07.989 --> 00:04:11.409
have put in place a fellowship of actors pretty
much immediately.

00:04:11.409 --> 00:04:16.109
But that hasn't been the case — or, at least,
if it is, Amazon is keeping quiet about it.

00:04:16.109 --> 00:04:17.780
"Alright then, you keep your secrets."

00:04:17.780 --> 00:04:19.060
"Huh?"

00:04:19.060 --> 00:04:22.630
So far, only one cast member for the series
has been confirmed.

00:04:22.630 --> 00:04:28.670
In July 2019, Variety reported that young
Australian actress Markella Kavenagh had been

00:04:28.670 --> 00:04:30.790
cast in a regular role on the series.

00:04:30.790 --> 00:04:34.930
According to the publication, Kavenagh will
be playing a character named Tyra.

00:04:34.930 --> 00:04:38.900
Curiously, no character with that name exists
in Tolkien's writing.

00:04:38.900 --> 00:04:43.750
The Walking Dead star Tom Payne also stirred
the waters back in early 2019 when he stated

00:04:43.750 --> 00:04:48.310
in an interview that he wanted to keep his
luscious locks partly because Amazon was "casting

00:04:48.310 --> 00:04:52.170
Aragorn," clearly implying that he wanted
a shot at the role.

00:04:52.170 --> 00:04:56.310
In another interview, Sir Ian McKellen was
asked about who else should play Gandalf if

00:04:56.310 --> 00:04:58.550
the wizard makes an appearance in the new
series.

00:04:58.550 --> 00:04:59.550
McKellen replied:

00:04:59.550 --> 00:05:00.860
"What do you mean another Gandalf?

00:05:00.860 --> 00:05:04.530
I haven't said yes because I haven't been
asked, but are you suggesting someone else

00:05:04.530 --> 00:05:05.570
is going to play it?"

00:05:05.570 --> 00:05:09.600
The return of Sir Ian McKellen would actually
make sense no matter when the show is set

00:05:09.600 --> 00:05:13.310
in Middle Earth history — Gandalf is thousands
of years old, after all.

00:05:13.310 --> 00:05:17.280
However, the return of any other actors from
the original Peter Jackson-helmed trilogy

00:05:17.280 --> 00:05:22.440
seems unlikely, if for no other reason than
the timeline the series will reportedly explore.

00:05:22.880 --> 00:05:27.400
While casting choices may be scarce so far,
several names have been dropped on the production

00:05:27.410 --> 00:05:28.530
end of things.

00:05:28.530 --> 00:05:32.300
Star Trek: Beyond co-writers JD Payne and
Patrick McKay have already been announced

00:05:32.300 --> 00:05:33.300
as the showrunners.

00:05:33.300 --> 00:05:34.860
In a statement, the pair announced:

00:05:34.860 --> 00:05:39.790
“We feel like Frodo, setting out from the
Shire, with a great responsibility in our

00:05:39.790 --> 00:05:40.790
care.

00:05:40.790 --> 00:05:42.620
It is the beginning of the adventure of a
lifetime.”

00:05:42.620 --> 00:05:47.360
Alongside Payne and McKay, it's also rumored
that Game of Thrones' Bryan Cogman and Breaking

00:05:47.360 --> 00:05:50.510
Bad's Gennifer Hutchison have seats in the
writers' room.

00:05:50.510 --> 00:05:55.390
Amazon has also locked down Jurassic World:
Fallen Kingdom filmmaker J.A. Bayona to direct

00:05:55.390 --> 00:05:57.060
the first two episodes of the series.

00:05:57.060 --> 00:06:02.620
In addition, Bayona will serve as executive
producer along with his partner Belén Atienza.

00:06:02.620 --> 00:06:06.950
Unsurprisingly, one other name that has continually
been brought up in relation to the series

00:06:06.950 --> 00:06:08.440
is Peter Jackson's.

00:06:08.440 --> 00:06:12.690
Rumors have waffled back and forth regarding
Jackson's potential involvement in the series.

00:06:12.690 --> 00:06:17.820
While he initially flat out denied being involved,
multiple reports have refused to confirm this

00:06:17.820 --> 00:06:22.490
fact, with Amazon's Jennifer Salke herself
stating that the lack of any specific news

00:06:22.490 --> 00:06:23.490
wasn't a negative.

00:06:23.490 --> 00:06:28.280
In addition, Jackson himself later added that
he was keen to help however he could, even

00:06:28.280 --> 00:06:30.380
expressing an interest in looking over the
scripts.

00:06:30.380 --> 00:06:33.900
At present, it's impossible to say what will
eventually happen.

00:06:33.900 --> 00:06:38.200
After all, Jackson wasn't even slated to direct
the Hobbit trilogy until the last minute.

00:06:38.200 --> 00:06:41.560
For now, though, he seems a peripheral influence
at best.

00:06:41.720 --> 00:06:47.070
With so much money and time being poured into
the project, it's probably fair to ask: just

00:06:47.070 --> 00:06:50.070
how many seasons are Amazon preparing to make?

00:06:50.070 --> 00:06:54.840
While specifics like exact episode count will
likely be unknown for quite some time, the

00:06:54.840 --> 00:06:59.550
studio is reportedly laying the groundwork
for a solid five seasons, along with a possible

00:06:59.550 --> 00:07:00.550
spinoff.

00:07:00.550 --> 00:07:04.250
While it's always gutsy committing to such
ambitious plans all at once, the promise of

00:07:04.250 --> 00:07:08.840
five entire seasons spent in Middle Earth
is encouraging, as it gives the showrunners

00:07:08.840 --> 00:07:13.270
time to tell the story without hustling in
order to meet artificial deadlines — a concern

00:07:13.270 --> 00:07:17.540
that infamously caused problems for Game of
Thrones' truncated final season.

00:07:17.540 --> 00:07:20.270
The possibility of a spinoff is intriguing,
too.

00:07:20.270 --> 00:07:24.271
Tolkien's stories often focus on a single
character for extended periods of time, with

00:07:24.271 --> 00:07:29.960
characters like Bilbo Baggins, Samwise Gamgee,
Beren and Lúthien, and Turin Turambar all

00:07:29.960 --> 00:07:34.290
stepping into the spotlight at various points
across the Middle Earth timeline.

00:07:34.290 --> 00:07:38.960
Spinning that long tapestry off into one or
more tie-in series is a concept with great

00:07:38.960 --> 00:07:42.280
potential, but only time will tell if the
idea has any merit.

00:07:43.440 --> 00:07:47.430
The question of where exactly the project
will be produced was officially answered in

00:07:47.430 --> 00:07:52.190
mid-2019, when it was announced that a "huge"
part of the show would be filmed in none other

00:07:52.190 --> 00:07:55.340
than Peter Jackson's old stomping grounds
of New Zealand.

00:07:55.340 --> 00:07:59.370
The Pacific island nation famously served
as the home to the bulk of the production

00:07:59.370 --> 00:08:03.970
of both The Lord of the Rings and Hobbit trilogies,
and Amazon has apparently decided that nowhere

00:08:03.970 --> 00:08:06.880
could quite beat the country's awe-inspiring
scenery.

00:08:09.280 --> 00:08:10.720
"Fair enough."

00:08:10.730 --> 00:08:14.760
Originally, Scotland had been considered as
a serious contender for filming.

00:08:14.760 --> 00:08:19.389
However, Radio New Zealand put forward the
claim that the Scots had lost out on the project

00:08:19.389 --> 00:08:22.380
due to the UK's "tumultuous Brexit situation."

00:08:22.380 --> 00:08:26.220
The return to the land of the Kiwis is rumored
to focus around the cities of Auckland on

00:08:26.220 --> 00:08:30.480
the northern island and Queenstown on the
southern one, with local facilities apparently

00:08:30.480 --> 00:08:31.930
already busy with pre-production.

00:08:31.930 --> 00:08:36.680
Auckland has already felt the impending arrival
of such a huge operation, as businesses in

00:08:36.680 --> 00:08:41.250
West Auckland have reportedly had to sign
non-disclosure agreements as they gear up

00:08:41.250 --> 00:08:44.920
to do brisk business while Amazon Studios
is in town.

00:08:44.960 --> 00:08:50.840
Way back in May 2018, a rumor sprung up that
suggested Amazon's Lord of the Rings series

00:08:50.860 --> 00:08:55.670
would focus on a younger version of everyone's
favorite Gondorian monarch: Aragorn.

00:08:55.670 --> 00:09:00.010
Since then, reports have obviously moved the
timing of the show back into Middle Earth's

00:09:00.010 --> 00:09:04.480
Second Age, which leaves it firmly out of
the reach of Aragorn's lifespan — after

00:09:04.480 --> 00:09:09.140
all, this is a stretch of time that ends nearly
three thousand years before the ranger was

00:09:09.140 --> 00:09:10.140
even born.

00:09:10.140 --> 00:09:13.720
The question of how Aragorn could fit into
a series that is purportedly set three millennia

00:09:13.720 --> 00:09:15.730
before his time is a curious one, though.

00:09:15.730 --> 00:09:19.779
Could he be merely be needed for an initial
framing sequence as he rules Gondor in the

00:09:19.779 --> 00:09:22.500
Fourth Age, before the show flashes back in
time?

00:09:22.500 --> 00:09:26.440
Or could it be that the earlier seasons will
start in the Second Age and ultimately end

00:09:26.440 --> 00:09:29.120
on Aragorn in his youth during the fifth season?

00:09:29.120 --> 00:09:31.670
And there's still the question of that spinoff
series, too.

00:09:31.670 --> 00:09:36.030
For now, however, how Aragorn is involved
in the series — if he is at all — is still

00:09:36.040 --> 00:09:37.040
a mystery.

00:09:37.360 --> 00:09:42.440
We live in an era where everyone from Marvel
and DC to The Walking Dead and Star Wars have

00:09:42.450 --> 00:09:46.610
built the concept of an "extended universe"
into their long term plans.

00:09:46.610 --> 00:09:51.710
Naturally, then, Amazon would be foolish not
to at least have one eye on an extended Middle

00:09:51.710 --> 00:09:55.640
Earth universe of their own, especially when
they're working with the dense and storied

00:09:55.640 --> 00:09:58.690
lore of one of the most popular world-builders
of all time.

00:09:58.690 --> 00:10:03.130
While specific franchise plans will take a
long, long time to unfold, Amazon has already

00:10:03.130 --> 00:10:07.760
announced one potential piece of universe-building
in the form of a new Lord of the Rings console

00:10:07.760 --> 00:10:09.900
video game that is already in development.

00:10:09.900 --> 00:10:13.720
The game does not appear to be directly linked
to the show, but that hardly disqualifies

00:10:13.720 --> 00:10:17.750
it as a part of the greater continuity that
Amazon is in position to propagate.

00:10:17.750 --> 00:10:22.060
Like the show, the game doesn't have a release
date yet, but it appears to be a free-to-play

00:10:22.060 --> 00:10:24.330
"massively multiplayer online" game.

00:10:24.330 --> 00:10:26.610
In a statement, Amazon Studios said:

00:10:26.610 --> 00:10:31.210
"[The game] will give fans around the globe
a new, immersive game experience for epic

00:10:31.210 --> 00:10:34.089
exploration of the vast world of Tolkien."

00:10:34.089 --> 00:10:38.540
Whether the game ultimately ties into anything
from the coming show or not, it would appear

00:10:38.540 --> 00:10:42.150
that Amazon's journey into Tolkien's world
has only just begun.

